# 03_graphrag_fruit_graph and 13_temporal_bitemporal_graphiti keep all
# their generated state inside their Neo4j docker volumes
# (neo4j-fruit-graph-data, neo4j-temporal-graph-data), so there is
# nothing on disk to ignore for either.

# 05_pii_erasure_replay - the redacted copy of the corpus, written during the
# erasure walkthrough. It is derived from corpus/, which IS committed.
05_pii_erasure_replay/corpus_redacted/

# 09_mcp_tools_and_scan - the tool pinning lockfile, written at approval time.
# Regenerated by 'main.py pin' and meaningless on another machine.
09_mcp_tools_and_scan/tools.lock.json

# 12_disk_ann_diskannpy - the on-disk ANN index. Binary, and the whole point
# of the exercise is that it is rebuilt rather than shipped.
12_disk_ann_diskannpy/data/

# Generic parquet catch-all for anything a pipeline drops outside the paths
# named above. Remove this line if you ever want to commit a fixture.
*.parquet

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Repository tooling output. The scripts themselves are committed; what they
project_contents.txt

# run_all_exercises.sh - test transcripts.
test_run.log
test_run.log.*
logs/

